# T16-R1 native probe supplement — self-pair rename + last-write rename
#
# Purpose: close the two native facts the original p16 matrix never probed:
#   1. standalone `RENAME TABLE a TO a` error class (contract assumed 1050,
#      review flagged it unverified);
#   2. last-write ordering of produced-then-consumed rename identities,
#      including the exact refusal error of a consumed source.
# The ALTER-form self-pair no-op was already probe-proven in
# p16_lifecycle_matrix.log (alter-rename-self); re-verified here for a clean
# single-version record.
#
# Fixture: disposable container `ds-t16r1-rename-probe` from local image
# `mysql:8.0` (reports 8.0.46, identical to the golden mysql80 anchor
# image mysql:8.0.46). Database `probe`, root/root. Removed after capture
# (`docker rm -f`; `docker ps -a` shows no residual).
#
# Commands executed via `docker exec ds-t16r1-rename-probe mysql -uroot
# -proot -e '<sql>'` (stderr shown verbatim; MYSQL_PWD warning filtered).

== version ==
SELECT VERSION();
VERSION()
8.0.46

== standalone self-repair rename ==
CREATE TABLE probe.rself (id INT);
RENAME TABLE probe.rself TO probe.rself;
rc=1
ERROR 1050 (42S01) at line 1: Table 'rself' already exists
-> standalone self-pair is a 1050 destination-occupied refusal. The
   destination binding really does observe the still-present source, so
   the rules-layer destination blocker is the faithful model.

== alter-form self-pair rename ==
ALTER TABLE probe.rself RENAME TO probe.rself;
rc=0
SELECT 'alter-self-rename-ok' AS outcome;
outcome
alter-self-rename-ok
SELECT COUNT(*) AS still_there FROM information_schema.TABLES
  WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA='probe' AND TABLE_NAME='rself';
still_there
1
-> ALTER-form self-pair is a proven no-op; no 1050, no rename, object
   stays. Syntax-form distinction is native, not modeled.

== last-write: produced-then-vacated destination ==
CREATE TABLE probe.a (id INT);
CREATE TABLE probe.d (id INT, dk INT);
RENAME TABLE probe.a TO probe.b, probe.b TO probe.c, probe.d TO probe.b;
rc=0
TABLE_NAME
b
c
rself
b_has_dk = 1      (b received d's shape after pair two vacated it)
c_has_dk = 0      (c carries a's original shape; d's shape NOT smeared)
-> all three pairs migrate; the destination freed by pair two is legal
   for pair three, and each destination receives the shape of the source
   as bound at its own pair.

== last-write: produced-then-consumed source ==
(state above reset: DROP TABLE probe.b, probe.c; CREATE TABLE probe.a (id INT);)
RENAME TABLE probe.a TO probe.b, probe.b TO probe.c, probe.b TO probe.a;
rc=1
ERROR 1146 (42S02) at line 1: Table 'probe.b' doesn't exist
SELECT GROUP_CONCAT(TABLE_NAME) FROM information_schema.TABLES WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA='probe';
a,rself
-> pair three's source `b` no longer exists (consumed by pair two):
   1146 source-missing refusal, whole statement rolls back, `a` survives,
   no phantom `b`/`c` is published.
